A||||6||Cheever2||Suggestions for Fiero event activities||||3||
Z||000000||Cheever2||07-19-2001||11:12 AM||||I am discussing with my local club about hosting an event here in the Houston area on or near New Years Eve, and have been trying to think up some activities.  So far, here are the ideas I have.  You may want to try some of these with your own club or event.  Let's have some more ideas, folks.<P><B>Finesse</B> driving games (low speed), like (1)-in a big parking lot, have the driver blindfolded and getting directions from the passenger for going through a maze of cones; (2)-who can stop with the tires closest to a special marked spot; (3)-a SLOW drag race, to see who can take the longest to go a short distance... if your wheels stop turning you're disqualified.<P>A Fiero trivia contest.  <P>A technical competition, like replacing a part in the quickest time.<P>"My other car" contest (not sure of the details on this, I need suggestions).<P>I'm a family man, and know how important it is to have something <B>for the kids</B> to do, so: (1)-Chinese fire drill; (2)-How many Fiero parts can you list (with a time limit); (3)-How many kids can you get into a Fiero.<P>Got any more?<BR><P>------------------<BR>- <I>Chuck Hodges</I> -<BR><A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay" TARGET=_blank> Fiero Parts Relay</A> administrator||||reg||3
Z||000001||stimpy||07-19-2001||11:40 AM||||Fiero valve cover derby...<BR>Finally a drag race where the four cylinders will whup tail on the sixes!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||07-19-2001||02:25 PM||||I have been going to corvair events for 20 years now (I'm 23) next weekend I'm heading to the national convention in Chicago.<P>The soul reason?? Autocross. At every corvair event I have ever been to they hold an autocross. The cars are classed by year and level of modification. Ever seen a corvair Van go around an autocross?<P>I would probably be more inclined to go to a fiero event if there were Autocrosses. A lot of people rave about fiero handling , pour tons of money into engine and suspension mods. Lets see how they do against other fiero's.<P>This is not for everyone obviously , but it is a great specticle to watch , it's fun to drive in, and competitive. As well it is safe.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||07-20-2001||09:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>Fiero valve cover derby...<BR>Finally a drag race where the four cylinders will whup tail on the sixes!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>And how about a Champion Spark Plug Challenge?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||3
Z||000004||Archie||07-20-2001||09:47 AM||||One Word...... BURNOUT CONTESTS<P>Well ok..... 2 words.<P>Archie||||reg||1
